repository-code: "https://github.com/cozuya/oeis-a057923"
abstract: >-
  An elementary proof and Lean 4 formalization that the greedy bitwise OR sequence
  OEIS A057923 satisfies a(n+2) > a(n) for every n >= 0. By Chris Ozols, with
  AI-assisted proof development and formalization. Verified with Lean 4.35.0
  using only the standard library. The sequence is credited to Larry Reeves
  (2000), and the conjecture to Robert Israel (2017).
  A bounded prior-art search found no earlier proof in the examined sources;
  no novelty, first-proof, priority, or official OEIS-status claim is made.
keywords:
